<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110012" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕψος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>, τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕψι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>height,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕψος κρεῖσσον ἐκπηδήματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1376
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ὕ. αἴρειν τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					404
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυπαρίττων ὕψη καὶ κάλλη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					625c
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕ. ἔχειν, λαμβάνειν,</span>
			rise some <i>height,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.91
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.13
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				2.75
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφ᾽ ὕψους [με] δισκοβόλησε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					336
				</span></i>
			 (Alexandria Troas): pl., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				44d
			</span></i>: abs. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕψος,</span>
			<i>in height,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῆκος, εὖρος,
				πλάτος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.50
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				178
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.372.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				22.1666<i>A</i>79
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMich.Zen.</u>
				38.12
			</span></i>, al. <span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς ὕψος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.13
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				155
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>summit, crown,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕ. ἀμαθίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					351d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σεμνότητος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mu.</u>
					398a12
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>sublimity, grandeur,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν λόγων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Metrod.
					<u>Herc.</u>
					831.8
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Longin.
				1.1
			</span></i>, al.: pl., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.4
			</span></i>.</div>
